    "transitionPlan": "opens on v04's final frame (see \"Opening frame\"); the chip \"Next: why does light spread after passing an edge or narrow opening?\" becomes the heading; the feature board fades. On \"Shine a laser through a narrow slit\" a camera change to the bench: the optical bench plate (`phys-y11-optical-bench-v1.png`, reused) with the laser module plate (`y12p-laser-module-v1.png`, from v02) at the left, the slide holder plate (`y12p-slide-holder-v1.png`, new) with a coded narrow slit at the centre, and the screen carrier plate (`phys-y11-screen-carrier-v1.png`, reused) at the right; a thin red beam. On \"side\" the screen shows a coded wide red central band with fainter bands either side (tag \"schematic\"); live readouts beside the screen (52 px) \"slit width 0.20 mm\", \"central band 13 mm\" (tag \"simulated\"). On \"prediction\" a 3 s `Countdown` beside two chips: \"narrower\" and \"wider\". On \"wider\" the coded slit narrows and the central band widens while the readouts tick \"0.10 mm, 26 mm\", then \"0.05 mm, 52 mm\"; the second chip ticks; red hand tag \"narrower slit, wider band\" and a red pen bracket across the widened band.\nboard change: the ripple tank plate (`phys-y11-ripple-tank-v1.png`, reused) for a beat, then a camera move to a coded top view of the water: teal straight wavefronts rolling right towards a dark grey barrier. On \"wide gap\" the gap is wide: fronts pass mostly straight, slightly curved at their ends. On \"edges\" the curved ends highlight. On \"about one wavelength wide\" the gap narrows to about one wavelength (a bracket \"gap ≈ λ\"); on \"barrier\" the fronts beyond it become semicircles reaching behind the barrier; pale grey hatching marks the region behind the barrier, tag \"spreads behind the barrier\". On \"diffraction\" a chip \"diffraction: waves spreading at an edge or through a gap\". Teal hand tags \"mostly straight\" (wide gap) and \"semicircles\" (narrow gap); teal pen arrow curling round behind the barrier.\nboard change to the Huygens stage: a straight vertical teal wavefront as a row of dots. On \"tiny source\" each dot pulses; on \"wavelet\" small teal circles grow from every dot. On \"the line touching the front of every wavelet\" a new straight front is drawn tangent to the circles' forward edges; tag \"new wavefront\". On \"neighbours on both sides\" two adjacent wavelets highlight, their overlapping sides shaded. On \"ahead\" the construction repeats a few steps; the front advances straight; tag \"open front: stays straight\". Teal hand tags \"every point a source\" on the dots and \"neighbours fill in\" on the overlapping sides; teal pen line tracing the new front.\non \"barrier in the way\" the Huygens stage adds a dark grey barrier with a gap; pale grey hatching marks the geometric shadow either side of a straight-through band. On \"on\" only the dots in the gap emit wavelets. On \"stays straight\" the middle of the new front is straight. On \"nothing beyond to fill in\" the edge wavelets highlight; teal hand tag \"no neighbours here\" with a teal pen arrow to the slit edge; on \"barrier\" their outer arcs curve into the hatched shadow. On \"A single edge\" a quick switch to single-edge mode: a half barrier, the front bending round its edge into the shadow. On \"Make the gap narrower\" the gap narrows step by step; on \"semicircle\" the front beyond is nearly a semicircle; teal hand tag \"narrow gap: wide spread\" and a teal pen ring round the single wavelet.\nboard change: a coded doorway outline with a bracket \"≈ 1 m\", and a navy chip \"λ (light) ≈ 500 nm\". On \"wide\" (the first) working (52 px): \"1 m / (500 × 10⁻⁹ m) = 2 × 10⁶ wavelengths\", framed; a red crossed chip \"1 / 500 = 0.002 wavelengths\" (caption \"nm → × 10⁻⁹ m\"). On \"far too small to notice\" the doorway's light beam passes with sharp edges; tag \"spreading negligible\". On \"Sound\" a sound wavefront (grey) with \"λ ≈ 1 m\" passes the doorway and spreads round the corner; on \"them